[EXTRACTION-CERT-001-DUAL-ISSUE]
UID: EXTRACT-001
TITLE: e200z4 Dual-Issue Pairing Rules Extraction

MANUAL_LOCATION: Chapter 1 (Microarchitecture Summary), Chapter 4 (Pipeline)

CURRENT_LLVM_IMPLEMENTATION:
Code_Location: llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCScheduleE200Z4.td
Model_Structure:
- 5-stage pipeline: IF, ID, EX, MEM, WB
- Dispatch ports: DIS0, DIS1
- Execution units: SU0, SU1, BU, LSU, MU, FPU/SPE
- IssueWidth = 2 (dual-issue)

DUAL_ISSUE_UNITS:
- SU0 (Simple Unit 0): Primary integer ALU
- SU1 (Simple Unit 1): Limited instructions (some can only use SU0)
- BU (Branch Unit)
- LSU (Load/Store Unit)
- MU (Multiply Unit)
- FPU/SPE (Floating-Point Unit / Signal Processing Extension)

MANUAL_EXTRACTION_REQUIRED:
1. Exact pairing rules from Chapter 4:
   - Which instruction types can pair?
   - What combinations are allowed?
   - Which instructions are restricted to SU0 only?
   - Pairing restrictions and conflicts

2. Dispatch port behavior:
   - DIS0 vs DIS1 usage rules
   - When can two instructions dispatch together?
   - Resource conflict resolution

3. Execution unit restrictions:
   - SU0-only instructions list
   - SU1 capability limitations
   - Resource sharing constraints

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
- [ ] Extract pairing rules table from manual
- [ ] Verify SU0-only restrictions match LLVM model
- [ ] Check DIS0/DIS1 usage matches manual
- [ ] Validate resource conflict rules
- [ ] Compare against PPCScheduleE200Z4.td itineraries

[EXTRACTION-CERT-001-TIMING]
UID: EXTRACT-002
TITLE: e200z4 Instruction Timing and Latency Extraction

MANUAL_LOCATION: Chapter 4 - Instruction Pipeline and Execution Timing

CURRENT_LLVM_LATENCIES:
From PPCScheduleE200Z4.td:
- Integer simple: 1 cycle (lines 61-68)
- Integer compare: 1-2 cycles (lines 86-93)
- Multiply: 4 cycles (lines 101-108)
- Divide: 34 cycles (lines 94-100)
- Load: 3 cycles (lines 169-175)
- Store: 3 cycles (lines 192-197)
- Branch: 1 cycle (lines 148-152)
- SPR ops: 1 cycle (lines 212-225)

MANUAL_EXTRACTION_REQUIRED:
1. Instruction timing tables from Chapter 4:
   - Base latency for each instruction class
   - Pipeline stage breakdown
   - Bypass path latencies
   - Load-to-use latency specifications

2. Dual-issue timing:
   - Latency when instructions pair vs unpaired
   - Resource conflict penalties
   - Dispatch timing constraints

3. Cache timing:
   - L1 cache hit latency
   - Cache miss penalty
   - Instruction cache (ICache) timing mentioned in code

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
- [ ] Extract instruction latency table from manual
- [ ] Verify each instruction class latency
- [ ] Check dual-issue vs single-issue timing differences
- [ ] Validate bypass path specifications
- [ ] Compare load-to-use latency (currently 4 cycles)

[EXTRACTION-CERT-004-VLE]
UID: EXTRACT-003
TITLE: e200z4 VLE (Variable Length Encoding) Specification

MANUAL_LOCATION: Chapter 3 (Instruction Model), VLE sections

CURRENT_LLVM_IMPLEMENTATION:
Code_Location: llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCInstrVLE.td
Register_Constraint: R0-R7 for 16-bit instructions (3-bit encoding)
Immediate_Predicates:
- s6imm: -32 to 31 (6-bit signed)
- u5imm: 0 to 31 (5-bit unsigned)
- u7imm: 0 to 127 (7-bit unsigned)
- u4imm: 0 to 15 (4-bit unsigned)

MANUAL_EXTRACTION_REQUIRED:
1. VLE encoding rules:
   - 16-bit vs 32-bit instruction selection
   - Register encoding constraints (3-bit = R0-R7)
   - Immediate value encoding limits
   - Boundary value handling

2. Instruction alignment:
   - 16-bit instruction alignment (2-byte)
   - 32-bit instruction alignment (4-byte)
   - Mixed-mode code boundaries
   - Instruction stream decoding

3. Register constraints:
   - Which instructions require R0-R7?
   - When can R8-R31 be used?
   - Register allocation implications

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
- [ ] Extract VLE encoding specification from manual
- [ ] Verify immediate value ranges
- [ ] Check register constraint rules
- [ ] Validate alignment requirements
- [ ] Compare with PPCInstrVLE.td implementation

[EXTRACTION-CERT-003-INTERRUPTS]
UID: EXTRACT-004
TITLE: e200z4 Interrupt Handling Extraction

MANUAL_LOCATION: Chapter 5 - Interrupts and Exceptions, Chapter 1.3.3

CURRENT_LLVM_IMPLEMENTATION:
Code_Location: llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCFrameLowering.cpp:1843-1913
Saves:
- LR (Link Register): ✓ Saved
- CR (Condition Register): ✓ Saved if used
- GPRs: ✓ Saved based on usage
- SPRs: ✗ Not saved (MISSING)
- FPRs: ? Need to check (e200z4 has SPE/FPU)
- FPSCR/SPEFSCR: ? Need to check

MANUAL_EXTRACTION_REQUIRED:
1. IVOR (Interrupt Vector Offset Register) table:
   - IVOR0: Critical interrupt
   - IVOR4: External interrupt
   - All other IVOR entries
   - Context save requirements per interrupt type

2. Exception handling:
   - Exception entry sequence
   - Automatic hardware saves (SRR0/SRR1)
   - Software-saved register requirements
   - Exception exit sequence (RFI/e_rfi)

3. Register save requirements:
   - Which SPRs must be saved?
   - FPR save requirements (e200z4 has SPE/FPU)
   - SPEFSCR save requirements
   - Differentiation by interrupt type

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
- [ ] Extract IVOR table from Chapter 5
- [ ] List register save requirements per interrupt type
- [ ] Identify which SPRs must be saved
- [ ] Check FPR/SPEFSCR save requirements for e200z4
- [ ] Verify RFI/e_rfi usage for VLE mode
- [ ] Compare with PPCFrameLowering.cpp implementation

[EXTRACTION-CERT-006-MEMORY]
UID: EXTRACT-005
TITLE: e200z4 Memory Barrier and Cache Coherency

MANUAL_LOCATION: Chapter 3 (Instruction Model), Chapter 1.2.2 (L1 Cache)

CURRENT_LLVM_IMPLEMENTATION:
Code_Location: llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCInstrInfo.td:2341-2358
Memory_Barriers: MSYNC, SYNC (may use MSYNC for both)
Cache_Model: L1 instruction cache mentioned (ICache functional unit)

MANUAL_EXTRACTION_REQUIRED:
1. Memory barrier semantics:
   - MSYNC instruction exact semantics
   - SYNC vs MSYNC usage
   - Memory ordering guarantees
   - Cache coherency requirements

2. Cache architecture:
   - L1 cache organization (from Chapter 1.2.2)
   - Cache line size
   - Cache coherency protocols
   - Instruction cache vs data cache structure

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
- [ ] Extract memory barrier specifications from manual
- [ ] Verify MSYNC vs SYNC semantics
- [ ] Check cache architecture details
- [ ] Validate cache coherency requirements
- [ ] Compare with PPCInstrInfo.td implementation

[EXTRACTION-CERT-005-EXCEPTIONS]
UID: EXTRACT-006
TITLE: e200z4 Exception Handling Extraction

MANUAL_LOCATION: Chapter 5 - Interrupts and Exceptions

CURRENT_LLVM_IMPLEMENTATION:
Code_Location: llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCScheduleE200Z4.td:94-100
Division_Latency: 34 cycles (modeled)
Exception_Path: Not modeled

MANUAL_EXTRACTION_REQUIRED:
1. Division exceptions:
   - Division by zero behavior
   - Exception type and priority
   - Exception latency
   - Software check requirements

2. Arithmetic exceptions:
   - Overflow detection
   - Exception generation
   - XER register behavior

3. Floating-point exceptions (e200z4 has FPU/SPE):
   - SPEFSCR (SPE Floating-Point Status and Control Register)
   - FPU exception types
   - Exception handling requirements

VALIDATION_CHECKLIST:
- [ ] Extract exception specifications from Chapter 5
- [ ] Verify division exception behavior
- [ ] Check FPU/SPE exception handling
- [ ] Identify exception latency specifications
